## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates practical implementation of data mesh principles, governance frameworks, and lineage automation on Google Cloud Platform.

## Key Concepts
- Domain-driven data ownership with BigQuery datasets
- Data Catalog metadata management and automated lineage
- IAM-based access control with Authorized Views
- CI/CD pipeline integration for schema drift prevention
- Cross-domain governance with policy-driven permissions

## Code Example
```javascript
function validateSchema(expectedSchema, actualSchema) {
  const expected = JSON.stringify(expectedSchema);
  const actual = JSON.stringify(actualSchema);
  return expected === actual;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Probes multi-tenant data integrity, privacy, and governance at scale, including schema drift handling, masking, and lineage.

## Key Concepts
- Schema registry in Cloud Storage and Drift detection in Dataflow/Beam
- Row-level security with BigQuery policies for per-tenant isolation
- Per-tenant DLP masking and quarantine of invalid data
- Data Catalog lineage and end-to-end observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-Beam DoFn skeleton for schema validation
class ValidateSchema extends DoFn {
  processElement(context) {
    const record = context.element;
    // load canonical schema from GCS
    // validate fields, types, requireds
    if (valid(record)) {
      context.output(record);
    } else {
      context.output(NOT_VALID, record);
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test schema drift in production without impacting traffic?
- How would you implement rollback across tenants if a schema change breaks downstream queries?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a candidate's ability to implement a straightforward streaming ingestion with validation, error handling, and rollback using familiar GCP primitives.

## Key Concepts
- Pub/Sub ingestion and Dataflow (Beam)
- JSON schema validation and field filtering
- BigQueryIO writes with insertId for idempotency and daily partitioning
- Dead-letter handling and Cloud Storage archival
- Lightweight testing and rollback planning

## Code Example
```javascript
function validate(record){
  if (typeof record.user_id !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_time !== 'string') return false;
  if (typeof record.event_type !== 'string') return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle late-arriving data and schema evolution?
- What monitoring and alerting would you add for bad records and rollback validation?
